5.5 Radiator Sizing — First‑Principles Calculation

The thermal radiator area required per tile is verified using the Stefan–Boltzmann law:

\dot{Q}_{\text{reject}} = \varepsilon \sigma A_{\text{rad}} T_{\text{rad}}^4,

where \varepsilon = 0.9 (high‑emissivity coating), \sigma = 5.6704 \times 10^{-8} W m⁻² K⁻⁴, A_{\text{rad}} = 0.15 m², and T_{\text{rad}} = 300 K (conservatively high). Evaluating:

\dot{Q}_{\text{reject}} = 0.9 \times 5.67 \times 10^{-8} \times 0.15 \times (300)^4 \approx 62 \text{ W}.

