A.8 Hill–Clohessy–Wiltshire Equations

For completeness, the linearised relative motion dynamics in a circular orbit of angular rate n = \sqrt{\mu / a^3} are (in the local‑vertical/local‑horizontal frame with x radial, y along‑track, z cross‑track):

\begin{aligned}
\ddot{x} - 2n\dot{y} - 3n^2 x &= \frac{F_x}{m}, \\
\ddot{y} + 2n\dot{x} &= \frac{F_y}{m}, \\
\ddot{z} + n^2 z &= \frac{F_z}{m}.
\end{aligned}
\tag{A.21}

These equations govern the relative motion between any two tiles in proximity and form the dynamical constraint in the SCP trajectory generation. For the 500 km SSO, n \approx 1.106 \times 10^{-3} rad s⁻¹.

---

A.9 Dipole–Dipole Magnetic Force and Potential

For completeness, the force on dipole 2 due to dipole 1, separated by \mathbf{r} = \mathbf{r}_2 - \mathbf{r}_1, is

\mathbf{F}_{12} = \frac{3\mu_0}{4\pi r^5} \Big[ (\mathbf{m}_1 \cdot \mathbf{r})\mathbf{m}_2 + (\mathbf{m}_2 \cdot \mathbf{r})\mathbf{m}_1 + (\mathbf{m}_1 \cdot \mathbf{m}_2)\mathbf{r} - \frac{5(\mathbf{m}_1 \cdot \mathbf{r})(\mathbf{m}_2 \cdot \mathbf{r})}{r^2}\mathbf{r} \Big],
\tag{A.22}

with \mu_0 = 4\pi \times 10^{-7} N A⁻². The magnetic potential energy from which this force derives is

\Phi_{\text{mag}} = \frac{\mu_0}{4\pi r^3}\left[\mathbf{m}_1 \cdot \mathbf{m}_2 - 3(\mathbf{m}_1 \cdot \hat{\mathbf{r}})(\mathbf{m}_2 \cdot \hat{\mathbf{r}})\right].
\tag{A.23}

