B.4 Formal AI Pipeline (Textual Description)

The Architect AI converts human‑language goals into formally verified assembly plans through a four‑stage pipeline:

```
Stage 1: NATURAL LANGUAGE INPUT
  Commander: "Assemble a 400 m³ ring habitat with a docking port
              on the north side and an observation cupola."

Stage 2: LLM → LTL TRANSLATION
  Pre‑trained Llama‑3 model (fine‑tuned on 10,000 paired natural‑
  language / LTL examples) generates candidate LTL specification:
    G(¬collision) ∧ F(G(ring_closed)) ∧ F(docking_port_north)
    ∧ F(cupola_installed) ∧ G(power_loop_closed)

Stage 3: SPIN MODEL CHECKING
  LTL formula parsed and verified against safety properties:
    ✓ Deadlock freedom: G(F(progress))
    ✓ Collision avoidance: G(d_ij ≥ r_safe)
    ✓ Connectivity: G(λ₂ ≥ λ_min)
    ✓ Power‑loop invariant: G(total_power ≥ total_load)
    ✓ Structural integrity: G(stable_truss)

Stage 4: DECISION
  ┌─ SPIN ACCEPTS ──► Plan passed to Foreman as sequence of
  │                    partial target graphs G*₀ ⊂ G*₁ ⊂ ... ⊂ G*_final
  │
  └─ SPIN REJECTS ──► Counterexample fed back to LLM.
                       Iterative refinement loop (max 3 cycles).
                       If still rejected → fallback to pre‑verified
                       graph‑grammar scaffold.
                       Guaranteed termination: finite state space
                       of valid LTL formulas; each iteration
                       eliminates ≥1 counterexample.
