C.6.3 Launch Architecture and Falcon 9 SSO Capacity

The widely cited 22,800 kg Falcon 9 payload figure applies to a 28.5° low‑inclination reference LEO, not to 500 km Sun‑synchronous orbit. For 500 km SSO, the Falcon 9 expendable payload capacity is approximately 4,700–4,800 kg. The Archimedes total mass of 16,515 kg therefore cannot launch on a single Falcon 9. The multi‑launch architecture is:

Launch Vehicle Payload Mass (kg)
L1 Falcon 9 (dedicated) Nucleus + Keeper Scaffold 105
L2–L7 Falcon 9 Transporter (× 6) A‑Tiles + Truss + PTMs ~2,500 each
L8 Falcon 9 (dedicated) Water + ECLSS pallets + crew systems ~7,500
Total 8 launches  ~16,515

Six Transporter rideshare missions at approximately $6 M each and two dedicated Falcon 9 launches at approximately $28 M each account for the $93 M launch budget line.

